====Usage notes====
{{m|nb|et|Et}} is normally unstressed. When the number one is emphasized, especially in contrast with two or more, the spelling {{m|nb|ett}} is used. Compare ''et hus'' (“a house”) and ''ett hus'' (“one house”).

Both spellings are permitted in ''et(t) eller annet'' and ''et(t) og annet'', regardless of stress. In ''et(t) eneste'', the choice normally follows the spoken stress. This differs from {{m|nb|en}}/{{m|nb|én}} and {{m|nb|ei}}/{{m|nb|éi}}, where the acute accent is optional even when the numeral is stressed.<ref>{{cite-web|url=https://sprakradet.no/spraksporsmal-og-svar/et-eller-ett/|title=Et eller ett?|work=Språkrådet|date=2024-01-01|accessdate=2026-10-27}}</ref>

